# Paths chezmoi removes from the target dir on every apply, relative to ~.
#
# Every entry is a rulesync project-scope output with no pass that generates it,
# so rulesync's own `delete: true` (scoped per pass) can never reclaim it.
# See README.md for the full pipeline.
#
# Do not add .claude/CLAUDE.md here. This file is applied on every apply, but the
# generate script only re-fires on a hash change, so the path would sit missing
# most of the time.

# codexcli rules, project scope. Replaced by ~/.codex/AGENTS.md (pass 3).
AGENTS.md

# cursor permissions, project scope. Replaced by ~/.cursor/cli-config.json (pass 2).
.cursor/cli.json

# claudecode rules, project scope. Replaced by ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (pass 3),
# which pass 3 now writes directly instead of through a symlink.
CLAUDE.md
